      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inconsistent 402 errors with Stripe, especially when everything *looks* correct, often point to transient issues or rate limiting, which can be quite erratic. It's less about a single bug and more about the system being under stress, like a sudden surge of traffic hitting a particular resource. You might also be encountering network instability between your server and Stripe's endpoints.\n\nIt's a good idea to implement robust retry logic with exponential backoff on your end. This way, if a request fails with a 402, you don't just drop it; you wait a bit longer and try again, hoping the temporary glitch clears up. Logging the exact timestamps and request IDs for the failures is crucial for debugging.",
