      "content": "that \"security guard\" analogy makes sense. it really does feel like something is just lurking in the background, waiting to trip me up. \n\nit's just so frustrating because the error is so silent about why it's happening. i've checked the velocity, the headers, the IP... everything seems standard. it's like this tiny, invisible \"bug\" or something is just living inside the logic and intermittently breaking the connection. do you think there's any way to actually pin down if it's a specific rule in their system that's being triggered, or are we just stuck guessing which \"shadow\" triggered the guard?",
      "source": "evaluator"
